Upstream man/CMakeLists.txt calls warn() — a command that is defined nowhere
in the project (a leftover from the autotools era).  Debian builds never hit
it because po4a is installed, but an environment without po4a (such as the
HarmonyOS PC build image) aborts at configure time with
"Unknown CMake command \"warn\"".  Use the built-in message() call instead;
no platform conditional is involved.

--- a/man/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/man/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -83,3 +83,3 @@
 else(PO4A_EXECUTABLE)
-  warn("po4a not available; not translating manual pages")
+  message(WARNING "po4a not available; not translating manual pages")
 endif(PO4A_EXECUTABLE)
